{{- /*
Builds the file Vercel reads through "bulkRedirectsPath" in vercel.json. It is
the Vercel counterpart of layouts/index.redirects (the Netlify _redirects file)
and layouts/index.aliases (the nginx map production uses). All three come from
the same page aliases, so they cannot drift apart.

Bulk redirects match an exact path and support no wildcards, so this file
reproduces the Netlify preview's exact-path behavior rather than production's
subtree matching.

Each alias is emitted twice, with and without a trailing slash. Vercel
normalizes trailing slashes itself, and emitting both forms makes the redirect
land whichever rule the CDN evaluates first.

An alias that differs from its target only by a trailing slash is skipped: it
would redirect to itself.

Two pages can claim the same alias, which is a content error but one the other
two pipelines tolerate -- Netlify and nginx both take the first rule and ignore
the rest. The first source wins here for the same reason, so a duplicate does
not reach Vercel and change which page the alias resolves to.
*/ -}}
{{- $redirects := slice -}}
{{- $seen := slice -}}
{{- range $p := .Site.Pages -}}
{{- $target := $p.RelPermalink -}}
{{- range .Aliases -}}
{{- $alias := strings.TrimSuffix "/" . -}}
{{- if and $alias (ne $alias (strings.TrimSuffix "/" $target)) -}}
{{- range $source := slice $alias (printf "%s/" $alias) -}}
{{- if not (in $seen $source) -}}
{{- $seen = $seen | append $source -}}
{{- $redirects = $redirects | append (dict
  "source" $source
  "destination" $target
  "statusCode" 301
  "preserveQueryParams" true) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $redirects | jsonify (dict "indent" "  ") -}}
